    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 2/2 tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the owner-create flow while keeping the flat `address` input working.\n\n**OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 the source for the generated DTOs:\n- Added `addressLine1` (optional, non-blank pattern) and `addressLine2` (optional) to `OwnerFields`, so both appear on the request DTO and the response `Owner` DTO.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, so a structured-only request passes bean validation. `city`/`telephone`/names stay required, keeping the contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Owner entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields (`address_line1`/`address_line2` columns) with getters/setters. MapStruct maps these by name automatically, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n**Schema DDL** \u2014 added the two nullable columns to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.normalizedAddress`) \u2014 the single point where the address is resolved on create now:\n- Prefers a non-blank `addressLine1`: normalizes `addressLine1` and (when present) `addressLine2`, stores the normalized values back on the owner (clearing a blank/absent line 2 to `null`), and returns the composed `address` = normalized line 1, with a single space + normalized line 2 appended when line 2 is present.\n- Otherwise falls back to the normalized flat `address` and clears the structured fields.\n- Returns `null` (\u2192 400) when neither form yields a usable address.\n\nThe composed value is stored via `setAddress`, so everything downstream that reads the stored address (and the shared `city`/`postcode` fields feeding the household hash, postcode validation and locality) sees the structured-derived value when present and the flat address otherwise.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 structured normalization/composition (`10 king st` \u2192 `addressLine1` and `address` both `10 KING STREET`) and continued acceptance of the flat form \u2014 both pass.",
